ork through the stages in order** Each page tells you what to write, shows the file as it is on the branch, and ends with the command that checks your work. Write the files yourself; checking out the branch is the answer key, not the lesson.\n4. **Compare when you are stuck** Every page links to the GitHub compare view for its stage, which shows exactly what changed.\n:::\n\n**Time:** about 20 minutes per stage. **You need:** a text editor, git, and the tools on the set-up page. The DogsBay XML editor is recommended but not required.\n\n## Where to go next {#where-to-go-next}\n\n:::cards\n- **[How the tutorial works](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/how-the-tutorial-works){icon=\"git-branch\"}**\n  Branches, diffs, the orphan root and the \"You are on\" line.\n\n- **[Set up your tools](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/set-up){icon=\"wrench\"}**\n  Install DITA-OT and the DogsBay XML command line.\n\n- **[Stage 00: Set up the project](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/part-1-topics/stage-00-setup){icon=\"play\"}**\n  Start building.\n:::\n","mdUrl":"https://dogsbay.ai/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/index.md"} ?? undefined;
